// =============================================================================
// Phase 14 coverage exclusion elfile (URG -elfile, applied at report time)
// =============================================================================
// Tracker : MMU-P14-ISSUE-022 (DUT code coverage closure)
// Policy : only structurally-unreachable objects are excluded here. No
//          functional/behavioral toggle or FSM transition is excluded.
//            Toggle  : reset nets (1->0 never occurs functionally) and DFT/perf
//                      enables tied off in verification.
//            FSM     : transitions whose ONLY code path is the asynchronous
//                      reset assignment in the state register (cpurst_b->IDLE).
//                      These are reported by URG as edges (e.g. WFG->IDLE) but
//                      have no functional next-state assignment; they require
//                      mid-test reset assertion while the FSM is mid-operation,
//                      which never occurs in functional runs. Every excluded
//                      transition was verified against the RTL combinational
//                      next-state block AND the state register to confirm no
//                      functional path exists (no abort-to-IDLE branch in the
//                      register, no IDLE assignment in the WFG/WFC/WT case).
//                      Functional uncovered transitions (e.g. PFU_CHK->PFU_DENY,
//                      IASID_WT->IASID_IDLE, l1itlb WFG->ABT, l1dtlb STATE_WFG
//                      ->STATE_IDLE, twu abort transitions) are NOT excluded
//                      and are tracked as closure work items under ISSUE-022.
// Review : Phase14 Closure Owner; second review required before final signoff
//          (doc/archive_merged_20260607/MMU_Phase14_SignoffMatrix.md S3/S5).
// Applied: wired into phase14_coverage_merge_parallel + scope URG reports via -elfile.
//
// Excluded signal classes (whole-signal toggle exclusion, both 0->1 and 1->0):
//   cpurst_b / rst_b / rst_n      -> reset nets; only deassert (0->1) at boot,
//                                    1->0 never occurs in functional runs.
//   pad_yy_icg_scan_en             -> DFT scan/ICG enable, tied to 0 in
//                                    functional mode; out of MMU verification scope.
//   hpcp_mmu_cnt_en                -> performance-counter enable, gated/tied in
//                                    verification; not a functional toggle target.
//
// Excluded FSM transition classes (reset-path-only, no functional next-state):
//   ct_mmu_tlboper tlbp/tlbr/tlbwi : WFG->IDLE (reset-only; WFG case has only
//                                    grant/stay assignments, no IDLE path).
//   ct_mmu_tlboper tlbwr           : TLBWR_WFG->IDLE, WRTAG->IDLE (reset-only).
//   ct_mmu_tlboper tlbiasid        : IASID_RD->IDLE, IASID_WFC->IDLE (reset-only).
//   ct_mmu_tlboper tlbiva          : IVA_CMP/RD/WR/WT->IDLE (reset-only).
//   mmu_l2tlb pfu_cur_st           : PFU_CHK->PFU_IDLE (reset-only; PFU_CHK has
//                                    only ->DENY/->OK, no IDLE path).
//
// Impact (measured 2026-06-14 on phase14_merged.vdb):
//   Toggle exclusions: DUT u_dut toggle 72.09% -> 72.34% (+0.25%).
//   FSM exclusions   : DUT u_dut FSM 80.90% -> ~86.1% (12 reset-only transitions
//                      removed; functional gaps remain, tracked under ISSUE-022).
//   line/branch/cond/assert unchanged by both exclusion classes.
//   The remaining toggle gap is address/ASID bit coverage driven by stimulus
//   distribution; the remaining FSM gap is functional abort/flush-during-miss
//   scenarios. Both are tracked separately under MMU-P14-ISSUE-022.
//
// Format: Synopsys URG elfile (Format Version 2). Each active (uncommented)
//         `Toggle <sig> "<decl>"` line excludes that signal in the preceding
//         INSTANCE block. Each active `Fsm <name> "<chk>"` + `Transition` pair
//         excludes that transition in the preceding INSTANCE block. ANNOTATION
//         lines are retained for source traceability.
//
// NOTE: Line/Cond/Branch/FSM waivers are tracked in the Phase14 Issue Tracker
// and doc/l2tlb_uvm_review/l2tlb_covp_waivers.md — they are NOT expressed in
// this elfile because URG requires a scope file (-cm_scope) for structured
// coverage types, and the current VDB was compiled without it.
// =============================================================================
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// L2TLB structural waivers (paper-tracked, NOT excluded from URG scoring):
//   mmu_l2tlb line  1382 : default FSM branch (2-bit FSM 4 states exhaust all)
//   mmu_l2tlb cond  553  : combo 0 1 1 (req=0 with write=1 impossible)
//   mmu_l2tlb cond  555  : combo 0 1 1 1 (req=0 with TLBop write impossible)
//   mmu_l2tlb cond  869  : combo 1 1 0 (final_par_fail = 1'b0 stub at line 865)
//   mmu_l2tlb cond  870  : combo 1 1 1 0 (same par_fail stub)
//   mmu_l2tlb cond  872  : combo 0 1 (same par_fail stub)
//   mmu_l2tlb cond  1167 : combo 1 1 0 1 (same par_fail stub)
//   mmu_l2tlb cond  1186 : combo 0 1 1 1 (false combinational: vld=0,miss=1)
// L1DTLB structural waivers (paper-tracked):
//   mmu_l1dtlb cond 315  : combo 1 1 0 1 1 (physically impossible: mb_entry_vld
//                           derives from state_r; state==WFC implies vld=1)
//   mmu_l2tlb fsm   pfu_cur_st PFU_CHK->PFU_IDLE (reset-only path, no functional)
//   mmu_l2tlb branch 1354 : default case (same reason as line 1382)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// CHECKSUM: "715530975 445175681"
// ANNOTATION: "ModuleName: mmu_l1dtlb"
INSTANCE: tb_top.u_dut.u_mmu_l1dtlb
//
Toggle cpurst_b "logic cpurst_b"
Toggle hpcp_mmu_cnt_en "logic hpcp_mmu_cnt_en"
Toggle pad_yy_icg_scan_en "logic pad_yy_icg_scan_en"

